UPDATE companies SET description='Kyocera Electronic Devices LLC operates from Fountain Inn, South Carolina, as the U.S. entity of KYOCERA AVX Components Corporation, a Japanese manufacturer of electronic components. The business serves as the local face of a global organization that develops, manufactures, and sells electronic devices worldwide, leveraging the parent company’s deep technical foundation and broad product portfolio.

The company manufactures a wide range of passive and electromechanical components. Its product lines include multilayer ceramic capacitors (MLCC), polymer and tantalum capacitors, board-to-board, FPC/FFC, wire-to-board, and memory card connectors, as well as timing devices such as crystal oscillators, SPXOs, and TCXOs. It also produces SAW filters, duplexers, and multiplexers, along with sensors and circuit protection devices. The operation spans design through volume production, though specific facility size and headcount are not disclosed.

Customers span automotive, consumer electronics, industrial, data-center, robotics, aerospace, and telecommunications sectors. In automotive, the company supplies AEC-Q200-qualified parts for battery-management systems (wBMS) and safety applications. Consumer applications include smartphones, wearables, gaming systems, and communication modules. Industrial and data-center customers use its components in AI servers, base stations, and general automation equipment.

The organization emphasizes a seamless flow from development to manufacturing and sales on a global scale. It highlights multi-band SAW solutions that save space in GNSS and positioning devices, ultra-miniature low-power timing devices for smart rings and medical instruments, and high-speed 0.5 mm pitch floating connectors for next-generation data transmission.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO/IATF']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Multilayer ceramic capacitor (MLCC) manufacturing", "Polymer capacitor manufacturing", "Tantalum capacitor manufacturing", "Board-to-board connector manufacturing", "FPC/FFC connector manufacturing", "Wire-to-board connector manufacturing", "Memory card connector manufacturing", "Crystal oscillator (SPXO) manufacturing", "Temperature-compensated crystal oscillator (TCXO) manufacturing", "SAW filter manufacturing", "SAW duplexer manufacturing", "SAW multiplexer manufacturing", "Sensor manufacturing", "Circuit protection device manufacturing"], "industries": ["Automotive (BLE/wBMS, safety, infotainment)", "Consumer electronics (smartphones, tablets, wearables, gaming)", "Industrial automation", "Data center and AI servers", "Robotics", "Aerospace and space", "Telecommunications (base stations, communication modules)"], "materials": ["Ceramic (MLCC)", "Polymer", "Tantalum", "Quartz crystal", "SAW substrate materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Global development-to-sales footprint", "Multi-band SAW filters and multiplexers for GNSS", "Ultra-miniature, low-power crystal oscillators (0.9 V drive)", "AEC-Q200 qualified automotive-grade components", "High-speed 0.5 mm pitch floating board-to-board connectors"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Fountain Inn, South Carolina -> db", "Parent company: KYOCERA AVX Components Corporation (Japan) -> db, /", "Product categories: Capacitors, Connectors, Timing Devices, SAW Devices, Sensors, Circuit Protection -> /", "Industries served: Automotive BLE/wBMS, Consumer, Industrial, Data Center, Robotics, Aerospace, Telecom -> /, db", "Certifications: ISO/IATF, RoHS, REACH, AEC-Q200 -> /", "Languages: Japanese, English, Korean, Chinese -> /", "YouTube channel mentioned -> /", "New product announcements (2025-2026) for timing devices, connectors, SAW devices -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "KYOCERA AVX Components Corporation ... has a strong technical foundation and rich lineup of electronic device related products, and develops, manufactures, and sells globally.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["REACH", "RoHS"], "languages": ["Japanese", "English", "Korean", "Chinese"], "social_links": ["https://www.youtube.com/@KyoceraElectronicDevices"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kyocera-electronic-devices-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='L. Sweet Lumber Company Inc. has operated from Providence, Rhode Island since 1885, when civil engineer Leprilete Sweet founded L. Sweet & Company in the city''s Olneyville section. Sweet soon purchased a wooden frame building from the Church of the Messiah, moved it to Harris Avenue for railroad access, and established the storefront that remains in use today. Now in its fifth generation, the business remains family‑owned and locally operated.

The company stocks a broad range of building materials: framing and finish lumber sourced from domestic and international forests, an extensive inventory of historical moulding profiles specific to the Providence area, interior and exterior doors, windows, skylights, hardwood flooring, TimberTech/Azek composite decking and railing, cedar shingles and clapboard siding, and general building supplies. A showroom displays samples and literature, and the staff provides blade sharpening, key cutting, and lock keying services. A fleet of trucks handles delivery across Southern New England.

L. Sweet Lumber serves contractors, homeowners, and historical‑restoration projects throughout Southern New England. The sales team offers personalized estimates, site visits, and product consultation, while the back office manages trade‑credit accounts and invoicing. The company also runs a contractor‑referral network for homeowners and supplies evaluated leads to its trade customers.

The firm emphasizes that its 140‑year commitment to service, selection, quality, and competitive pricing drives its approach.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Lumber sales", "Moulding & millwork", "Doors & windows", "Flooring", "Decking & railing", "Siding & roofing", "Building materials supply", "Delivery", "Trade credit", "Estimates & sales support", "Site visits & product consultation", "Contractor referrals", "Blade sharpening", "Key cutting", "Lock keying", "Showroom displays", "Online moulding catalog", "Sourcing of specialty & custom made products"], "industries": ["Building construction", "Residential construction", "Historical restoration"], "materials": ["Framing lumber", "Finish lumber", "Cedar", "Hardwood", "Composite decking (TimberTech/Azek)", "Moulding profiles", "Cedar shingles", "Clapboard siding"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fleet of trucks for on-time delivery", "Trade credit accounts", "Contractor referral network", "Historical moulding profiles in stock", "Blade sharpening, key cutting, and lock keying services"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1885 by Leprilete Sweet -> db, /about-us", "Headquarters Providence, RI -> db, /about-us", "Family-owned, fifth generation -> /about-us", "Products: framing/finish lumber, moulding, doors, windows, flooring, decking, siding, roofing, building materials -> /", "Historical moulding profiles specific to Rhode Island -> /", "TimberTech/Azek dealer -> /", "Services: delivery, trade credit, estimates, site visits, contractor referrals, blade sharpening, key cutting, lock keying, showroom -> /services", "Industries: building & construction industry Southern New England -> /", "Commitment to service, selection, quality, competitive pricing for 140 years -> /, /about-us", "Fleet of trucks for on-time delivery -> /services", "Trade credit accounts -> /services", "Contractor referrals -> /services", "Online moulding catalog -> /services", "Sourcing specialty/custom products -> /services", "Showroom displays -> /services"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Serving the building & construction industry throughout Southern New England with quality lumber and building products, since 1885.", "founded_year": "1885", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='l-sweet-lumber-company-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Douglas, Wyoming, L&L Fabrication Inc operates as an ASME-certified pressure vessel shop serving the Rocky Mountain region.

The shop holds ASME U, R, and VR stamps, allowing it to fabricate, repair, and alter coded pressure vessels to specification. Its capabilities include coded vessel fabrication and repair, engineering support, piping fabrication up to 72 inches in diameter, certified crane and rigging services, customized hauling, and on-site field services for oil and gas operations. Processes encompass coded welding, plasma cutting of conductive metals such as steel, stainless steel, aluminum, brass, and copper, as well as heavy industrial fabrication of skidded process equipment, separator vessels, and gas production equipment.

L&L Fabrication primarily serves the oil and gas sector, including pipeline operations, gas production facilities, and upstream and midstream projects. The company provides custom metal fabrication in Wyoming and industrial fabrication contractor services throughout Colorado, supporting customers with heavy industrial fabrication and on-site support.

The company states its vision is to become the provider of engineering, fabrication, and technical services in the Rocky Mountain region, distinguished by uncompromising quality standards, advanced innovation, and customer-centric solutions. Core values cited include integrity, innovation, quality, and efficacy, with an emphasis on meeting deadlines and maintaining site safety.', certifications=ARRAY['ASME U Stamp','ASME R Stamp','ASME VR Stamp','ASME BPVC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Coded Vessel Fabrication and Repair", "VR Stamps Oil & Gas Field Service", "Premier Oil & Gas Field Services", "Piping Fabrication up to 72\" Diameter", "Certified Crane and Rigging Services", "Engineering", "Customized Hauling", "Plasma Cutting", "Coded Welding", "Pressure Vessel Repair and Maintenance", "Skidded Process Equipment Fabrication", "Separator Vessel Fabrication", "Gas Production Equipment Fabrication", "Pipeline Fabrication", "Industrial Steel Fabrication"], "industries": ["Oil and gas", "Pipeline", "Gas production", "Upstream and midstream", "Industrial fabrication"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Brass", "Copper"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ASME U, R, and VR stamps for coded vessel work", "Piping fabrication up to 72-inch diameter", "Certified crane and rigging services", "Field services for oil and gas operations", "Customized hauling and on-site support in Wyoming and Colorado"], "facts_used": ["Location: Douglas, Wyoming -> db", "ASME U, R, VR stamps held -> /", "Services: coded vessel fabrication, piping up to 72\", crane and rigging, engineering, customized hauling -> /", "Processes: coded welding, plasma cutting (steel, stainless steel, aluminum, brass, copper) -> /", "Industries served: oil and gas, pipeline, gas production, upstream/midstream -> /", "Geographic service: Wyoming and Colorado -> /", "Vision statement and core values -> /", "Pressure vessel repair and maintenance offered -> /", "Skidded process equipment, separator vessels, gas production equipment fabricated -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "L&L Fabrication is an ASME Code vessel shop Holding U, R, and VR stamps.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='l-l-fabrication-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='L.L.Bean was founded in 1912 by Leon Leonwood Bean in Brunswick, Maine. From its start, the company focused on offering high-quality products at reasonable prices.

Today the retailer carries thousands of items across men''s, women''s, and children''s clothing; footwear including the signature Bean Boots; outdoor gear for hunting, camping, and fly fishing such as tents, backpacks, sleeping bags, kayaks, and canoes; as well as furniture, bedding, and luggage. Products are described as lab- and field-tested, and all are backed by a customer service reputation the company calls legendary.

Its customer base spans outdoor enthusiasts, families, and home shoppers seeking durable goods.

The company emphasizes free shipping on orders over $75, a rewards program, and a branded credit card that provides free returns. Its stated differentiation rests on product durability and a service pledge that has become a hallmark of the brand.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Lab and field testing of outdoor gear", "Direct-to-consumer order fulfillment"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Free shipping on orders over $75", "Legendary customer service pledge", "Lab- and field-tested outdoor gear", "L.L.Bean Mastercard with free returns", "L.L.Bean Rewards loyalty program"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1912 by Leon Leonwood Bean -> /", "Headquarters in Brunswick, Maine -> db", "Offers thousands of high-quality products at reasonable prices -> /", "Free shipping with $75 purchase -> /", "Product categories: men''s/women''s/kids'' clothing, boots, shoes, slippers, outdoor gear (tents, backpacks, sleeping bags, kayaks, canoes), furniture, bedding, luggage -> /", "Lab- and field-tested outdoor gear -> /", "Legendary customer service claim -> /", "Stores in Freeport, Maine and other locations -> /", "L.L.Bean Mastercard for free returns -> /", "L.L.Bean Rewards program -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "unclear", "type_evidence": "Founded in 1912 by Leon Leonwood Bean, L.L.Bean offers thousands of high-quality products at reasonable prices with Free Shipping with $75 purchase.", "founded_year": "1912", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='l-l-bean' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LA Woodshop operates a 7,000-square-foot workshop and creative space in downtown Los Angeles, California. The business is structured as a collective of woodworking educators and professionals, though no founding year or individual founders are disclosed in public materials.

The facility combines education, production, and retail functions. It runs woodworking classes ranging from one- or two-day weekend workshops to longer-form advanced courses, and provides bench space for independent makers. On the production side, the shop offers CNC machining and laser engraving services to customers who supply their own lumber, and accepts custom furniture commissions built by its instructors and students. A retail area sells finished furniture, student projects, and branded merchandise.

The client base spans hobbyists seeking skill development, corporate groups booking team-building workshops, and buyers of custom wood furniture or CNC/laser services. Corporate events are marketed as customized workshops for team cohesion.

The collective model distinguishes the operation by embedding instruction and community access alongside fabrication services, positioning the shop as both a learning environment and a production resource for local makers and businesses.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Woodworking instruction (weekend workshops, multi-session courses)", "CNC machining", "Laser engraving", "Custom furniture fabrication", "Corporate team-building workshops", "Bench space / open shop access", "Retail sales (furniture, merchandise)"], "industries": ["Education", "Corporate Training", "Furniture", "Woodworking Services"], "materials": ["Lumber", "Wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["7,000 sq ft workshop in downtown Los Angeles", "Collective of woodworking educators and professionals", "On-site CNC machining and laser engraving services", "Custom furniture commissions by instructors and students", "Corporate team-building workshops"], "facts_used": ["Location: 1535 Paloma St., Los Angeles, CA 90021 -> /", "7,000 sq ft workshop and creative space -> /", "Collective of woodworking educators and professionals -> /", "Woodworking classes (weekend workshops, longer-form) -> /", "CNC and laser engraving services offered -> /", "Custom furniture commissions -> /", "Corporate team-building events -> /", "Retail shop selling furniture, projects, merchandise -> /", "Headquarters city/state: Los Angeles, California -> db", "Capabilities list includes CNC & LASER ENGRAVING Services -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We offer CNC and laser-engraving right here in the heart of Los Angeles.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='la-woodshop' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LAPCO Manufacturing, Inc. was founded in 1989 in Morgan City, Louisiana. The company began producing flame-resistant (FR) workwear for industrial workers facing arc flash and flash fire hazards.

The company manufactures a range of FR garments including jackets, coveralls, shirts, jeans, outerwear, and accessories. Products are made from materials such as 100% cotton, 88/12 cotton/nylon blends, 95/5 cotton/spandex blends, 13-ounce cotton denim, and inherent knit fabrics. Operations are based at a headquarters facility on Glenwood Street in Morgan City, where the company handles design, production, and distribution. LAPCO also offers custom coverall orders with a reputation for fast turnaround.

Primary customers work in oil and gas, electric utility, refining, and petrochemical industries. The company sells through a network of distributors and directly via its e-commerce site, serving both men and women with modern, comfort-focused designs. Trade association membership underscores its industry standing.

LAPCO emphasizes a service-oriented approach, promoting excellent customer support, pain-free inventory acquisition for distributors, and responsive custom order fulfillment. The brand positions itself on safety, reliability, and purpose, aiming to deliver workwear that helps wearers feel safe, work smart, and look good.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Flame-resistant garment manufacturing", "Custom coverall production", "Distributor program support", "Direct-to-consumer e-commerce"], "industries": ["Oil and gas", "Electric utility", "Refining", "Petrochemical"], "materials": ["100% Cotton", "88/12 Cotton/Nylon Blend", "95/5 Cotton/Spandex Blend", "13oz. 100% Cotton Denim", "6oz. Inherent Knit", "7oz. 100% Cotton", "7oz. 88/12 Blend"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Excellent customer service and pain-free inventory acquisition for distributors", "Fast turnaround on custom coverall orders", "Safety-compliant FR workwear for arc flash and flash fire protection", "Modern, comfortable designs for men and women", "Trusted by industrial workers since 1989"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989 -> db", "Headquarters Morgan City, Louisiana -> db", "Industries served: oil and gas, electric utility, refining, petrochemical -> /", "Products: FR workwear (jackets, coveralls, shirts, jeans, outerwear) -> /", "Materials: 100% Cotton, 88/12 Blend, 95/5 Cotton Spandex Blend, 13oz Cotton Denim, 6oz Inherent Knit -> /", "Custom coverall orders with fast turnaround -> /", "Built on Service: excellent customer service, pain-free inventory acquisition -> /", "Social media presence: Twitter, Facebook, Pinterest, Instagram, YouTube -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Workers in the oil and gas, electric utility, refining, and petrochemical industries have utilized LAPCO Premium Workwear products since 1989.", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "",