"Direct LED replacement for miniature lamps and indicators -> /", "Company described as LED lamp manufacturer -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a proud American company that has been manufacturing LED products in the USA since 1983!", "founded_year": "1983", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "8Z410", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ledtronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='La France Industries, operating as LaFrance Fabrics, is headquartered in La France, South Carolina. The company was founded in 1996 as P&A Industrial Fabrications, LLC, a subsidiary of the P&A Group, LLC. Its roots trace to the textile heritage of Roxboro, North Carolina, where velvet looms have operated for over a century.

The company manufactures premium woven fabrics on velvet, jacquard, and drop-stitch looms. Product lines include paint roller fabrics (1/4" to 3/4" pile height), grip tape roll covering, microfiber fabrics for cleaning, heel pads for automotive carpeting, polyester filtration fabrics, ski climbing skins, flat fabrics, and woven drop-stitch fabrics for inflatable boats, body boards, and airline lift bags. Finishing capabilities encompass tentering, heat setting, coating, napping, shearing, and slitting. The operation exports to ten countries and relies on a workforce whose weavers and technicians average 30 years of experience, with leadership totaling 160 combined years in the textile industry.

Customers span automotive, paint roller manufacturing, textile, microfiber cleaning, filtration, ski and snow sports, inflatable boat production, body board manufacturing, aviation (airline lift bags), and government/military sectors requiring Berry Compliance certification. The company serves both commercial and governmental end users.

LaFrance Fabrics differentiates itself through Berry Compliance certification for velvet, jacquard, and drop-stitch looms, a Lean Manufacturing culture with regular 5S and Kaizen events, and a staff PhD who drives collaborative product development. The firm emphasizes long-term supply-chain partnerships and continuous improvement.', certifications=ARRAY['Berry Compliance certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Velvet loom weaving", "Jacquard loom weaving", "Drop-stitch loom weaving", "Tentering", "Heat setting", "Coating", "Napping", "Shearing", "Slitting", "Product development (PhD-led)", "Berry Compliance certification", "Lean manufacturing (5S, Kaizen)"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Paint roller manufacturing", "Textile", "Microfiber cleaning products", "Filtration", "Ski and snow sports", "Inflatable boats", "Body boards", "Aviation (airline lift bags)", "Government/military (Berry Compliance)"], "materials": ["Polyester", "Velvet", "Microfiber", "Pile fabrics"], "equipment": ["Velvet looms", "Jacquard looms", "Drop-stitch looms"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Berry Compliance certification for velvet, jacquard, and drop-stitch looms", "Lean Manufacturing with 5S and Kaizen continuous improvement", "PhD-led product development for custom applications", "Workforce averaging 30 years of weaving and technical experience", "Exports to 10 countries"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 -> db", "Headquarters La France, SC -> /about-us", "Part of P&A Group, LLC -> /about-us", "Products: paint roller fabrics, grip tape, microfiber, heel pads, polyester filtration, ski climbing skins, flat fabrics, drop stitch fabrics -> /about-us", "Processes: velvet looms, jacquard looms, drop-stitch looms, tentering, heat setting, coating, napping, shearing, slitting -> /about-us", "Berry Compliance certification -> /about-us", "Exports to 10 countries -> /about-us", "Workforce average 30 years experience, leadership 160 combined years -> /ab