UPDATE companies SET description='Lance Industries was founded in 1985 in Hartford, Wisconsin, where it began producing vacuum massage tumblers with design input from Family Farms Meats and the engineering staff at LMI Manufacturing. The company introduced the first American-made meat tumbler, built specifically for the needs of the U.S. meat industry.

The company manufactures four models of commercial vacuum meat tumblers — the LT-5 (50 lb capacity), LT-15 (200 lb), LT-30 (500 lb), and LT-60 (1,000 lb) — featuring variable-speed drives, digital timers, built-in vacuum systems, and wheels on all units for mobility through standard 32-inch doors. Drums are constructed from thicker-gauge steel, and each unit includes a removable lid with a metal-detectable gasket for cleaning and food safety. More than 3,000 tumblers have been installed worldwide.

Lance equipment serves meat markets, grocery stores, butcher shops, delis, restaurants, meat processors, and meat-alternative processors. Customers cited in company materials include Haun''s Meat & Sausage, Bardini''s Country Smokehouse, Bob''s Processing, Hudson Meats, and Quality Cut Meats, which reported a used tumbler still operating after 34 years.

Lance Industries emphasizes durability, reliability, and U.S.-based technical support with a fully stocked repair department. The company is a member of the American Association of Meat Processors (AAMP) and the Wisconsin Association of Meat Processors (WAMP), exhibiting at both national and state conventions to stay close to customer needs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Vacuum tumbling", "Meat marination", "Meat tenderizing", "Protein extraction", "Uniform coating and breading application", "Flavor infusion", "Accelerated curing and processing", "Yield improvement", "Equipment service and repair", "Spare parts supply", "Technical support"], "industries": ["Meat processing", "Delis", "Butcher shops", "Grocery stores", "Restaurants", "Meat alternative processing", "Meat markets"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["LT-5 vacuum meat tumbler (50 lb capacity)", "LT-15 vacuum meat tumbler (200 lb capacity)", "LT-30 vacuum meat tumbler (500 lb capacity)", "LT-60 vacuum meat tumbler (1,000 lb capacity)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First American-made meat tumbler designed for U.S. meat industry", "Wheels on all units for mobility through standard 32-inch doors", "U.S.-based customer service with fully stocked repair and parts department", "Variable-speed control and digital timer for precise marination cycles", "Metal-detectable gasket for food-safety compliance"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1985 in Hartford, Wisconsin -> /about-us", "First American-made meat tumbler -> /about-us", "Designed with Family Farms Meats and LMI Manufacturing -> /about-us", "Four models: LT-5, LT-15, LT-30, LT-60 -> /", "3,000+ tumblers worldwide -> /", "Features: variable speed, digital timer, built-in vacuum, wheels, removable lid, metal-detectable gasket -> /", "Industries served: meat markets, grocery stores, butcher shops, delis, restaurants, meat processing facilities, meat alternative processors -> /", "Customer testimonials: 