UPDATE companies SET description='Larson Cable Trailers, Inc. is based in Huron, South Dakota. Founded in 2000 by Rick Larson, the company began as an offshoot of his underground utilities business, Larson Digging Inc. Unable to find a trailer that could lift cable reels, “figure 8,” and rewind cable efficiently, Larson built his own patented cable fiber installation trailer.

The company manufactures patented cable fiber installation trailers designed to handle reel lifting, figure‑8 layout, and rewinding in a single unit. Its product line includes the original Larson Cable Trailer and, since 2024, the Drive Trailers series. The division also runs an online parts store supplying trailer components, manuals, and warranty service.

Primary customers are public and private contractors, rural telephone cooperatives, electric cooperatives, and city municipalities involved in fiber‑optic and power infrastructure projects. The trailers are used for burying cable, fiber‑optic installation, and electrical line construction across the United States.

The business was started to solve a real‑world problem Larson faced daily: the need for a versatile, durable trailer that could increase crew efficiency. The patented design aims to let crews lay more cable in less time by combining multiple functions into one piece of equipment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable fiber installation trailer manufacturing", "Reel handling solutions", "Trailer parts distribution", "Warranty services", "Online parts store operation", "Drive Trailers product line manufacturing", "Fiber optic handling solutions"], "industries": ["Fiber optic", "Power", "Telecommunications", "Electrical utilities", "Municipal government", "Rural telephone cooperatives", "Electric cooperatives", "Public/private contractors"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Patented cable fiber installation trailer design", "Single trailer handles reel lift, figure\u20118, and rewind", "Built from hands\u2011on underground utility experience", "Online parts store for components and warranty service", "Backed by Felling Trailers\u2019 full\u2011line manufacturing resources"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2000 by Rick Larson -> db, /about", "Headquarters in Huron, South Dakota -> db", "Patented cable fiber installation trailer -> /", "Acquired by Felling Trailers in early 2024 -> /about", "Operates as separate division of Felling Trailers -> /about", "Added Drive Trailers product line in early 2024 -> /about", "Serves public/private contractors, rural telephone co-ops, electric cooperatives, city municipalities -> /about", "Online trailer parts store -> /, /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Larson Cable Trailers revolutionized the industry as the original creator of the patented cable fiber installation trailer.", "founded_year": "2000", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='larson-cable-trailers-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Latest Metalworks operates from Murrieta, California, in Riverside County. Founded nearly two decades ago, the company has built a reputation for large-scale metal fabrication across Southern California and nationally.

The shop provides full-program fabrication from engineering review through final delivery. Core processes include laser cutting with an AMADA fiberoptic laser, waterjet cutting on an OMAX machine, forming and bending via an Amada press brake, 8-axis tube bending and rolling, and LADBS-certified welding. Additional capabilities cover engineering and CAD using Solidworks, secondary finishing, and a dedicated packaging department for kitted shipments. The facility handles production runs, structural assemblies, exhibit structures, prototype programs, and architectural metalwork.

Clients span automotive OEM, industrial, architectural, EV and solar, and R&D sectors. Notable references include Temeka Group for retail, museum, and commercial projects; the City of Oceanside Water Department for plant maintenance fabrication; Inokinetic for product manufacturing; Tube Bending Technology, an aerospace supplier; and V&T Tooling Inc. for tooling components.

