UPDATE companies SET description='LCS Precision Molding, Inc. operates from Waterville, Minnesota, where it has provided custom plastic injection molding for more than 50 years. The company began as a small molding operation created to meet a specific customer need and grew from a single machine into a full-service manufacturer with 15 presses and end-to-end project support.

The company runs 15 injection molding presses with clamping forces from 22 to 400 tons and shot capacities up to 27 ounces. In-house engineering assists with part design, resin selection, and design-for-manufacturing feedback, while mold development is coordinated through domestic and international tooling partners. Secondary operations include assembly, custom packaging, kitting, stocking programs, and specialized shipping, allowing LCS to handle short-run orders as well as long-term production programs.

LCS serves industries such as fenestration, motorsports, recreational products, furniture, electronics, water filtration, retail infrastructure, and specialized industrial applications. Customers range from OEMs needing precision housings and components to manufacturers of building products, outdoor equipment, and fluid-handling systems.

LCS emphasizes a one-partner approach from concept through delivery, backed by ISO 9001:2015 certification and an on-time delivery record exceeding 95 percent. The company highlights flexible production capacity, personalized project management, and U.S.-based manufacturing with access to both domestic and overseas tooling resources as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic injection molding", "Engineering and design support", "Design for manufacturing feedback", "Resin selection assistance", "Mold development and maintenance", "Domestic and international tooling coordination", "Secondary operations", "Assembly", "Custom packaging", "Kitting", "Stocking programs", "Specialized shipping", "Project management", "Real-time ERP production tracking"], "industries": ["Fenestration", "Motorsports", "Recreational Products", "Furniture", "Electronics", "Water Filtration", "Retail Infrastructure", "Specialized Industrial Applications"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["15 injection molding presses (22\u2013400 ton)", "Shot capacity up to 27 ounces"], "volume": "Short runs to long-term production programs", "lead_time": "Under 5 weeks average build-to-order lead time", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One partner from concept to delivery (engineering, tooling, production, assembly, logistics)", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system", "On-time delivery rate above 95%", "15 presses from 22 to 400 tons supporting short runs and long-term programs", "U.S.-based manufacturing with domestic and international tooling options"], "facts_used": ["Location: Waterville, Minnesota -> /about-us", "Founded as small molding operation over 50 years ago -> /about-us", "15 presses, 22-400 ton capacity, shot sizes up to 27 oz -> /", "Engineering support, mold development, secondary operations -> /", "Industries: fenestration, motorsports, recreational products, furniture, electronics, water filtration, retail infrastructure, specialized industrial -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified by T\u00dcV S\u00dcD America -> /", "On-time delivery >95% -> /", "Average build-to-order lead time under 5 weeks -> /", "One-partner approach from concept to delivery -> /", "U.S.-based manufacturing with domestic and international tooling -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our production floor includes 15 injection molding presses ranging from 22 to 400 tons.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lcs-precision-molding' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='LeVic Plastics was founded in 1971 by Leslie "Bill" Stober and Vic Mathis in a garage in Grandview, Missouri, initially focusing on prototype molding for manufacturers. The company incorporated and moved to a dedicated facility in Grandview as demand grew, with Ron Knight becoming a partial owner before taking sole ownership in 1990. Bob Knight later purchased the business, continuing its customer-focused manufacturing approach.

Today LeVic operates as a full-service custom injection molder with in-house tooling and secondary operations under one roof. The facility runs 10 Shibaura (Toshiba) presses ranging from 55 to 250 tons, capable of holding tolerances to ±0.001 inch and producing runs from a single piece to over 100,000 parts. Services span mold design, CNC machining of aluminum and steel tooling, insert molding, color matching, and secondary processes such as sonic welding, pad printing, hot stamping, assembly, and packaging.

The company serves manufacturers across medical, aerospace, electronics, oil and gas, industrial automation, machinery, and packaging sectors. Engineers, buyers, and supply chain teams engage LeVic for prototype development, low-to-mid volume production, and ongoing manufacturing support, often consolidating multiple suppliers into a single point of accountability.

LeVic emphasizes its "One-Vendor Advantage," combining engineering-driven DFM support, certified quality systems (ISO 9001:2015 and AS9100D), no minimum order quantities, and quote turnaround within two to three business days to simplify supply chains and ensure repeatable quality from first article through long-term production.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100D']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Mold design (SolidWorks, Mastercam, full 3D CAD)", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM) review", "In-house tooling: aluminum molds", "In-house tooling: steel molds", "Prototype tooling", "Production tooling", "CNC machining for tooling", "Mold modifications", "Custom plastic injection molding (55\u2013250 ton presses)", "Insert molding", "Color matching", "Sonic welding", "Hot stamping", "Pad printing", "Assembly services", "Packaging", "Engineering review and manufacturability recommendations", "Prototype & production tooling design"], "industries": ["Medical", "Aerospace", "Electronics", "Oil & Gas", "Industrial Automation", "Machinery", "Packaging"], "materials": ["Commodity thermoplastics", "Engineering-grade thermoplastics", "Reinforced materials", "Insert molded components", "Custom color-matched formulations"], "equipment": ["10 Shibaura (Toshiba) injection molding presses (55\u2013250 ton)"], "volume": "1 to 100,000+ pieces", "lead_time": "2\u20133 business days for quotes", "tolerances": "\u00b10.001 inch", "built_on": ["One vendor manages mold design, tooling, molding, and secondary operations", "No minimum order quantities", "ISO 9001:2015 and AS9100D certified quality systems", "Tolerances held to \u00b10.001 inch", "Standard quotes returned in 2\u20133 business days"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1971 -> db, / (homepage)", "Founders Leslie ''Bill'' Stober and Vic Mathis -> /about", "Headquarters Grandview, Missouri -> db, /about", "Ownership history: Ron Knight sole owner 1990, Bob Knight purchased later -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 and AS9100D certi