UPDATE companies SET description='Leprino Foods Company began in 1950 as a small family-run grocery store in Denver, Colorado, when Mike Leprino Sr. started making mozzarella cheese by hand in a back room for his family''s corner market. The business incorporated as Leprino Cheese Manufacturing Company in the 1960s and adopted the Leprino Foods Company name in the 1970s, remaining family-owned throughout its growth.

Today the company is the world''s largest producer of mozzarella cheese and a manufacturer of whey protein, lactose, micellar casein, and other dairy ingredients. Its proprietary processes include the patented "Same Day Dice" method that turns fresh milk into cheese in four hours, and Quality-Locked Cheese that is individually quick-frozen to preserve peak flavor. Operations span manufacturing facilities on three continents, including a 640,000-square-foot plant in Lemoore, California, with over 1,100 employees, and a global headcount exceeding 5,000. Products reach more than 70 countries.

Leprino serves food and nutrition brands worldwide, from major pizza chains and foodservice operators to consumer-packaged-goods manufacturers. A strategic alliance with Dairy Farmers of America secures milk supply, while joint ventures in Europe, Latin America, and Asia Pacific extend its reach. The company also entered the direct-to-consumer market with the Ascent® Protein brand.

The Leprino Difference—rooted in the founder''s credo "Leprino Quality is a way of life"—emphasizes quality, service, competitive price, and ethics. The company''s stated purpose is to sustainably feed and nourish families globally, guided by a climate-action commitment targeting greenhouse-gas neutrality by 2050.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Mozzarella cheese production (pasta filata)", "Whey protein manufacturing", "Lactose production", "Micellar casein production", "Quality-Locked Cheese (IQF)", "Same Day Dice process", "Research and development (pilot plant)", "Global supply chain management", "Nutrition ingredient manufacturing", "Cheese dicing and shredding", "Frozen cheese processing", "Dairy ingredient blending", "Private label manufacturing", "Co-manufacturing"], "industries": ["Food and beverage", "Dairy", "Pizza and foodservice", "Nutrition and health ingredients", "Consumer packaged goods", "Retail (B2C)", "Food manufacturing"], "materials": ["Milk", "Mozzarella cheese", "Ricotta", "Scamorze", "Pizza cheese", "Bacio\u00ae cheese", "Whey protein", "Lactose", "Micellar casein", "Dairy ingredients"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Patented \"Same Day Dice\" process (fresh milk to cheese in four hours)", "Quality-Locked Cheese (individually quick-frozen to lock in flavor)", "World''s largest mozzarella cheese producer", "Family-owned since 1950", "Global manufacturing footprint on three continents"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1950 in Denver, Colorado -> /about", "Founder Mike Leprino Sr. started making mozzarella in family grocery store -> /about", "Family-owned company -> /about", "World''s largest mozzarella producer -> /", "Leading manufacturer of whey protein, lactose, micellar casein -> /", "Patented Same Day Dice process (4 hours milk to cheese) -> /about", "Quality-Locked Cheese (IQF) -> /about", "Over 5,000 employees worldwide -> /about", "Lemoore plant: 640,000 sq ft, 1,