UPDATE companies SET description='Levine Contract Furniture Group was founded in 1973 by Harvey Levine at a desk in the Pan Am Building on 42nd Street in New York City. In 1975, John Calvano joined and expanded the sales territory using his personal vehicle.

The firm acts as a contract furniture dealer and specifier, representing multiple manufacturing partners to furnish corporate, healthcare, education, and retail environments. It maintains an inventory of in-stock products that can ship within 48 hours, ranging from small orders to 50,000-square-foot office installations.

Levine serves corporate workplaces, healthcare facilities, educational institutions, and retail spaces. Its portfolio includes open-plan collaboration areas, private offices, conference rooms, huddle rooms, cafés, reception areas, and training rooms. The company emphasizes technology management and durability for educational settings and clinical, public, and professional furnishings for healthcare.

The company differentiates itself through rapid fulfillment of stocked items, a deep understanding of regulated environments such as healthcare, and the ability to deliver bespoke solutions with integrated technology and material selection. Its New York City showroom offers virtual and in-person tours, and the firm provides continuing education units (CEUs) and contract pricing support.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Contract furniture specification", "In-stock furniture fulfillment", "Custom furniture design and procurement", "Power and data integration", "Privacy pod installation", "Space planning and design", "Project management", "Showroom tours", "Continuing education (CEUs)", "COM/COL management", "Contract pricing", "Sustainability consulting"], "industries": ["Corporate", "Healthcare", "Education", "Retail"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "48 hours for in-stock products", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-stock furniture shipping in as quickly as 48 hours", "Custom furniture and architectural elements with integrated technology and material choice", "Deep expertise in healthcare, education, and corporate environments", "Represents multiple manufacturing partners", "New York City showroom with virtual and in-person tours"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1973 by Harvey Levine -> db", "Founded at a desk in the Pan Am Building on 42nd Street -> db", "John Calvano joined in 1975 -> db", "Family-owned -> db", "Headquartered in New York City -> db, /", "Markets contract furniture for corporate, healthcare, education, retail -> /", "In-stock products ship in as quickly as 48 hours -> /", "Custom furniture and architectural elements with technology integration -> /", "Power and data solutions offered -> /", "Privacy pods offered -> /", "Showroom in New York City -> /", "Offers CEUs, COM/COL, contract pricing -> /", "Serves corporate, healthcare, education, retail -> /", "Deep understanding of healthcare space -> /", "Bespoke solutions with material choice -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "LCFG markets contract furniture designed for corporate, healing, learning, and retail environments.", "founded_year": "1973", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='levine-contract-furniture-group' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Liberate Medical is based in Crestwood, Kentucky. The company develops and manufactures the VentFree Respiratory Muscle Stimulator, a non-invasive neuromuscular electrical stimulation device designed to contract the abdominal wall muscles in synchrony with exhalation during mechanical ventilation.

The VentFree system uses proprietary stimulation technology that can be initiated from the first day of mechanical ventilation, even while patients are sedated or delirious, without requiring patient cooperation. The device is CE marked for sale throughout the European Economic Area and holds U.S. FDA Emergency Use Authorization to reduce disuse atrophy of the abdominal wall muscles, which may shorten the duration of mechanical ventilation in adult patients, including those with COVID-19.

Liberate Medical serves the critical care and respiratory care markets, targeting hospitals and intensive care units that manage mechanically ventilated patients. Clinical evidence from a pilot randomized controlled trial published in Critical Care (2019) demonstrated that patients receiving VentFree stimulation experienced shorter mechanical ventilation duration and reduced ICU length of stay compared to placebo.

The company positions its technology as a breakthrough approach to preparing patients for weaning from day one of ventilation, aiming to reduce abdominal muscle atrophy—a factor associated with weaning failure and delayed extubation—and potentially lower morbidity, mortality, and healthcare costs.', certifications=ARRAY['CE MARKED']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Non-invasive neuromuscular electrical stimulation", "Respiratory muscle stimulation synchronized with exhalation", "Medical device manufacturing", "Clinical research and trial execution"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Critical care", "Respiratory care", "Hospital equipment", "Healthcare"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["VentFree Respiratory Muscle Stimulator"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Non-invasive neuromuscular electrical stimulation synchronized with exhalation", "Therapy can begin day one of mechanical ventilation without patient cooperation", "CE marked for the European Economic Area", "FDA Emergency Use Authorization for reducing abdominal wall muscle disuse atrophy", "Pilot RCT showed reduced mechanical ventilation duration and ICU length of stay"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Crestwood, Kentucky -> db", "Product: VentFree Respiratory Muscle Stimulator -> /", "Technology: non-invasive neuromuscular electrical stimulation synchronized with exhalation -> /", "CE marked for European Economic Area -> /", "FDA Emergency Use Authorization for reducing disuse atrophy of abdominal wall muscles -> /", "Pilot RCT published in Critical Care 2019 showing reduced ventilation duration and ICU stay -> /", "Targets mechanically ventilated patients, including COVID-19 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "VentFree Respiratory Muscle Stimulator uses proprietary non-invasive neuromuscular electrical stimulation to contract the abdominal wall muscles in synchrony with exhalation during mechanical ventilation.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["CE marked for European Economic Area", "FDA Emergency Use Authorization"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='liberate-medical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Lincoln Electric Products Co. was founded in 1949 in Union, New Jersey, as a manufacturer of high‑quality electrical distribution equipment serving the tri‑state area. The company remains family‑owned and operated, guided by the core values established by its founder, Irving Leff.

The company produces a full range of highly customizable electrical distribution equipment, including switchboards and integrated electrical systems. All manufacturing takes place in the United States under an ISO 9001:2015‑certified quality management system. The firm emphasizes precision craftsmanship, offering an industry‑two‑year warranty on all equipment, and targets lead times as short as four weeks through experienced project managers and engineers who adapt designs to site‑specific challenges.

The company differentiates itself through its family‑owned heritage, domestic manufacturing, and a commitment to continuous improvement and on‑time delivery. President Matthew Leff leads a mission focused on collaborative relationships and well‑engineered, high‑quality electrical equipment.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical distribution equipment manufacturing", "Switchboard manufacturing", "Custom electrical system design", "Project management", "Engineering design", "Integration services", "Quality management (ISO 9001:2015)"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "As short as four weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Industry-leading two-year warranty on all equipment", "Target lead times as short as four weeks", "All equipment manufactured in the USA", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "Family-owned and operated since 1949"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1949 -> /about", "Family-owned and operated -> /about", "Founder Irving Leff -> /about", "Headquarters in Union, New Jersey -> db", "Manufactures electrical distribution equipment -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality", "Two-year warranty on all equipment -> /", "Lead times as short as four weeks -> /", "All equipment manufactured in USA -> /", "President Matthew Leff -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We build a full range of highly customizable electrical distribution equipment.", "founded_year": "1949", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lincoln-electric-products-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Lincoln Industries Manufacturing of WI, LLC operates from Menomonee Falls, Wisconsin. The privately held metal finishing company traces its roots back more than seven decades, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed. Ownership remains private, and the company does not name its founders in available materials.

The company specializes in precision electroplating and has been expanding its in-house coating capabilities. Its product portfolio includes a range of truck components such as exhaust systems, bumpers, internal cab parts, grab bars, engine components, emblems, and heat management solutions. In 2025, Lincoln Industries launched Fourth Wall, a new division focused on LED display solutions for sports venues, businesses, and outdoor environments. The company describes itself as the largest and most diverse privately held metal finishing operation in North America, though facility size, headcount, and production volumes are not disclosed.

Lincoln Industries serves customers across agriculture, automotive, appliances, motorsports, powersports, oil and gas, tools, and heavy-duty truck markets.

