UPDATE companies SET description='Lone Mountain Biotechnology and Medical Devices, Inc. was founded in December 2008 by Dr. Robert L. Garnick in Las Vegas, Nevada. Dr. Garnick brought over 25 years of experience Genentech''s regulatory and quality organizations, where he was responsible for the approval of more than 17 drugs. The company began as a consulting practice leveraging that expertise to assist pharmaceutical and biotechnology clients with drug and device development.

The firm provides consulting services across clinical and CMC regulatory affairs, quality control and assurance, and cGXP compliance (including GCP, GLP, and GMP). It also operates a prototype device development capability using AutoCAD for design and Haas CNC equipment for machining. Services span drug development portfolio evaluations, IND/NDA/BLA preparation, manufacturing site evaluations, comparability studies, FDA advisory committee support, and due diligence reviews for investors. The company additionally offers clinical trial design, pre-clinical studies, process sciences, analytical methods development, and biosimilar development support.

Lone Mountain serves the pharmaceutical, biotechnology, and medical device industries. Its client base ranges from large pharmaceutical companies to early-stage start-ups, as well as investors seeking due diligence on manufacturing capabilities and CMC sections of regulatory filings. The company has facilitated numerous FDA Type C meetings and has worked with three clients on biosimilar development programs, including cell line and process development.

The company differentiates itself through a network of senior consultants—former Genentech colleagues—who collectively have brought over 17 drugs to market. This "Dream Team" provides rapid resolution of complex drug development issues, FDA meeting facilitation, and biosimilar pathway strategy. The prototype machining capability allows clients to move from design to G-code and physical prototypes in-house.', certifications=ARRAY['GMP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Drug development project portfolio evaluation", "Regulatory affairs: IND, NDA, BLA, CTX preparation and review", "Promotional material review", "Manufacturing site evaluation for regulatory applications", "Comparability study design and execution", "FDA advisory committee planning and rehearsal", "Validation strategy for analytical methods and manufacturing processes", "cGXP, cGMP, cGLP inspectional support", "Strategy development for new manufacturing sites", "FDA/EMA review interaction management", "Medical device development strategy and execution", "AutoCAD device design to G-code", "Prototype device design and development", "Prototype to manufacturing strategic planning", "Due diligence reviews of manufacturing capabilities and capacities", "Due diligence reviews of CMC sections of CTDs", "Warning letter and consent decree resolution", "Clinical trial design and implementation", "Pre-clinical studies", "Process sciences", "Analytical methods development", "GXP compliance", "Stability studies", "Virology and microbiology consulting"], "industries": ["Pharmaceutical", "Biotechnology", "Medical Device"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Haas CNC machines", "AutoCAD"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Network of senior consultants with 25 years at Genentech and 17 drug approvals", "Facilitation of FDA Type C meetings for early-stage drug development", "Biosimilar development experience including cell line and process development", "In-house prototype device development with AutoCAD and Haas CNC equipment", "Due diligence reviews for investors on manufacturing capabilities and CMC sections"], "facts_used": ["Founded December 2008 by Dr. Robert L. Garnick -> /", "Headquarters Las Vegas, Nevada -> /", "Provides consulting services in regulatory affairs, quality, cGXP compliance -> /", "Prototype device development with AutoCAD and Haas CNC equipment -> /", "Services include drug development portfolio evaluation, IND/NDA/BLA preparation, manufacturing site evaluations, comparability studies, FDA advisory committee support, due diligence reviews -> /", "Serves pharmaceutical, biotechnology, medical device industries -> /", "Clients include large pharmaceutical companies, start-ups, investors -> /", "Facilitated FDA Type C meetings -> /", "Biosimilar development experience with three clients -> /", "Network of consultants with Genentech experience and 17 drug approvals -> /", "Certification: GMP -> db", "Equipment: Haas CNC machines, AutoCAD -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Lone Mountain Biotechnology also provides experimental and Prototype level device development capability with state of the art AutoCAD and CNC prototyping capability using Haas equipment.", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='lone-mountain-biotechnology-and-medical-devices-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
