UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1998 in Baton Rouge, Louisiana, Louisiana School Equipment Company (LSEC) has spent over 25 years providing furniture solutions to educational and public institutions across the state.

These include space planning with CAD drawings, product specification and recommendation, ADA-compliant layout design, installation scheduling and coordination, project consultation, and assistance with state contract purchasing. As a licensed Louisiana Specialty Contractor, the firm handles projects of all sizes from its Baton Rouge headquarters and a network of representatives statewide.

The company serves public and private K‑12 schools, colleges and universities, government agencies, and architecture and design professionals throughout Louisiana. Its client base also includes businesses seeking workspace furnishings. LSEC maintains professional memberships in organizations such as NSSEA/EDspaces, LASBO, AIA Louisiana, and the Associated General Contractors to stay connected to the education and facility planning communities.

LSEC’s stated mission is to exceed customer service expectations by delivering quality products, expert service, and professional installation. The company emphasizes relationships, innovative solutions, and a commitment to excellence to create environments where people can learn, work, and succeed. Its differentiators include statewide coverage, a licensed contractor status, and decades of specialized experience in educational environments.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Space planning and CAD drawings", "Product recommendations and specifications", "ADA-compliant layout design", "Installation scheduling and coordination", "Project consultation and support", "State contract purchasing assistance", "Furniture sales and distribution", "Professional installation"], "industries": ["K-12 education", "Higher education", "Government", "Architecture and design", "Business/commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Statewide service with headquarters in Baton Rouge and representatives across Louisiana", "Licensed Louisiana Specialty Contractor", "Over 75 years of combined experience in educational furniture sales, installation, and customer service", "Space planning and CAD drawings included in project services", "State contract purchasing assistance for public agencies"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1998 -> db, /", "Headquarters in Baton Rouge, Louisiana -> db, /", "Over 75 years combined experience -> /", "Licensed Louisiana Specialty Contractor -> /", "Services: space planning, CAD drawings, product recommendations, ADA-compliant layouts, installation scheduling, project consultation, state contract purchasing assistance -> /about", "Industries served: public & private K-12 schools, colleges & universities, government agencies, architects & design professionals -> /about", "Professional memberships: NSSEA/EDspaces, LASBO, LHSAA, AIA Louisiana, NIGP Louisiana, Louisiana Library Association, Associated General Contractors, Louisiana School Food Service Association, Louisiana College & Technical College System, Louisiana School Facility Managers Association -> /about", "Mission statement -> /", "HON Ignition Seating Series product line -> /", "Statewide service with representatives across Louisiana -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Providing furniture solutions throughout Louisiana since 1998", "founded_year": "1998", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='louisiana-school-equipment-company-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Louisiana Structured Cabling, LLC operates from Lake Charles, Louisiana, and was founded in 1986 by Matthew Theriot, who serves as president. Theriot brought over 40 years of experience designing and installing custom cabling solutions for industrial and commercial businesses across the United States before establishing the company.

The firm specializes in the design and installation of structured cabling systems, including fiber optic backbone cabling and precision splicing, Category 6 and 6A copper cabling, and closed-circuit television systems. Its service portfolio extends to communication room design and installation, underground directional boring and conduit installation, core drilling for vertical and horizontal cable paths, and professional display mounting for operations centers and offices. The company holds a Louisiana state license (#62337) and maintains memberships with BICSI, ISNetworld, and DISA.

Louisiana Structured Cabling serves commercial and industrial clients throughout Louisiana, including high-security facilities, corporate offices, and operations centers. The company emphasizes a personal commitment to the state''s growth and provides services for businesses requiring mission-critical data infrastructure and advanced surveillance systems.', certifications=ARRAY['BICSI Member','ISNetworld Member','DISA Member','LA License #62337','NDAA Compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fiber optic cabling and splicing", "Category 6/6A structured cabling", "CCTV system installation", "Security camera installation", "Communication room design", "Communication room installation", "Directional conduit boring", "Conduit installation", "Core drilling for cable paths", "TV/monitor installation"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Fiber optic cable", "Cat-6 cable", "Cat-6A cable"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lifetime guarantee on new horizontal cabling installations", "NDAA Compliant", "BICSI Member", "ISNetworld Member", "DISA Member"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 -> db", "Headquarters Lake Charles, Louisiana -> db", "Founder/president Matthew Theriot with 40+ years experience -> /", "Services: fiber optic, category cabling, CCTV, camera installation, communication room design/install, conduit boring/install, core drilling, TV/monitor installation -> /", "Lifetime guarantee on new horizontal cabling installations -> /", "BICSI Member, ISNetworld Member, DISA Member, LA License #62337, NDAA Compliant -> /", "Serves commercial and industrial clients across Louisiana -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "provides fiber optic and category cabling services for businesses and industries across Louisiana", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='louisiana-structured-cabling-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Lusk Scandia Woodworks operates from Coon Valley, Wisconsin, where Mike Lusk began working with wood in 1985 and turned the craft into a full-time profession in 2000. Mike’s background includes early training through the Vesterheim Norwegian American Museum and a gold medal in woodcarving awarded in 1992.

The shop produces custom handcrafted woodworks inspired by Scandinavian design, including cabinets, doors, shelves, tables, trunks, bent-wood boxes, bowls, ornaments, figurines, and plaques. Every item is made by hand using basswood for pieces intended to be painted or rosemaled, as well as a variety of hardwoods for stained finishes. The Lusks prepare surfaces to a smooth finish but leave final finishing to the customer, and they also offer woodcarving instruction at the Vesterheim Museum and Norskedalen Heritage Center.

Testimonials cite purchases of mirrors, trays, and bowls from Wisconsin, Texas, and beyond.

The company distinguishes itself through a direct lineage to Norwegian immigrant craft traditions—Mike’s grandfather was a woodcarver and his mother a Vesterheim Gold-medalist in rosemaling. Pieces are designed to be well made, beautifully designed, and built to last, with lead times of 10 to 16 weeks for custom orders.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry and furniture making", "Hand carving (figure, ale bowl, dragonstil, relief)", "Bent wood box construction", "Surface preparation and sanding", "Woodcarving instruction"], "industries": ["Home decor", "Furniture", "Giftware", "Woodworking", "Scandinavian folk art"], "materials": ["Basswood", "Hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "10-16 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Completely one-of-a-kind, handmade projects", "Scandinavian design heritage rooted in Norwegian immigrant traditions", "Items prepared for customer-applied finishes (basswood for rosmal/paint, hardwoods for stain)", "Woodcarving instruction at Vesterheim Museum and Norskedalen Heritage Center", "Gold medal in woodcarving from Vesterheim (1992)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1985, professional since 2000 -> db and /", "Location Coon Valley, WI -> db and /", "Owners Mike and Becky Lusk -> /", "Products: custom cabinets, doors, shelves, tables, trunks, bowls, ornaments, figurines, plaques -> /", "Materials: basswood, various hardwoods -> /", "Processes: handcrafted, woodcarving, sanding -> /", "Lead time 10-16 weeks -> /", "Ships to all 50 states -> /", "Teaching at Vesterheim Museum and Norskedalen Heritage Center -> /", "Gold medal woodcarving 1992 -> /", "Family-owned -> /", "Scandinavian design heritage -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Together we make a variety of finely hand crafted Scandinavian inspired wood pieces.", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": 