UPDATE companies SET description='MEDiSURG is based in Indianapolis, Indiana, and was founded in 2002 by John Weymouth. Weymouth, a biomedical engineering technologist, began his career as a medical equipment repairman in the U.S. Army at Fort Detrick, Maryland, before spending years at Alcon in product management and sales. He launched MEDiSURG to focus exclusively on ophthalmic surgical equipment.

The company provides full-service repair, preventive maintenance, and calibration for phaco and vitrectomy surgical systems, along with a supply of new and refurbished parts and complete refurbished units. It also offers equipment leasing and a buy-back/trade-in program. Training programs cover system setup, component replacement, diagnostics, and preventive maintenance, delivered through in-person workshops, live Zoom sessions, and on-demand courses. MEDiSURG operates with a team of six technicians and support staff from its Indianapolis location, where it maintains an inventory of parts and refurbished Alcon Centurion, Constellation, and Infiniti systems.

Its customers include hospitals, ambulatory surgery centers (ASCs), and physician offices that perform cataract and retinal surgeries. The company services platforms such as the Alcon Centurion, Constellation, and Infiniti phacoemulsification systems, as well as vitrectomy machines.

MEDiSURG positions itself as an independent, third-party alternative to manufacturer-tied service programs, emphasizing unbiased recommendations and a customer-focused approach. The founder’s background in product development and sales at Alcon informs the company’s technical depth, and the firm highlights its 75+ years of combined ophthalmic expertise among staff.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Ophthalmic equipment repair", "Preventive maintenance", "Phacoemulsification system service", "Vitrectomy system service", "Refurbished equipment sales", "Equipment leasing", "Parts supply", "Technical training (in-person, live virtual, on-demand)", "Biomedical technician training", "Surgical staff training", "System setup and calibration", "Component replacement", "Diagnostics and troubleshooting", "On-site service", "Remote consultation", "Video-link support", "24/7 emergency service", "Equipment deinstallation", "Data sanitization"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Ophthalmology", "Ambulatory Surgery Centers", "Hospitals", "Physician Offices"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Alcon Centurion", "Alcon Constellation", "Alcon Infiniti", "KUSA (CUSA) machines", "Phaco surgical equipment", "Vitrectomy systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "24-hour emergency response", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Independent, third-party service provider (not tied to manufacturers)", "24/7 emergency service with 24-hour response", "On-site, remote, and video-link support options", "In-house refurbishment of phaco and vitrectomy systems with warranty", "Technician training programs awarding CEU credits and certificates"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2002 -> /about", "Founder John Weymouth -> /about", "Team of six employees -> /about", "Headquarters Indianapolis, IN -> /about", "Services: repair, preventive maintenance, parts, refurbished sales, training -> /about, /services", "Brands: Alcon Centurion, Constellation, Infiniti -> /about", "24/7 emergency service -> /ab