UPDATE companies SET description='The company presents itself as “Proudly Built in Montana” and references “40 Years Exhaust Innovation,” suggesting the founders brought decades of prior experience to the venture, though individual founders are not named on the site. Ownership structure is not disclosed.

The company designs and manufactures performance exhaust systems for late-model trucks and SUVs. Its product line includes cat-back dual exhaust kits, side-exit and turndown systems, and stainless steel exhaust tips. The core technology is a patented pulse chamber intended to eliminate in-cab drone while preserving exhaust flow for horsepower gains. All components carry a limited three-year warranty, with stainless steel products covered by a limited lifetime warranty. No facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures are published.

MPI’s applications target the Ford F‑150 (2021‑2026) and the Jeep Gladiator (2020‑2026 3.6L), offering both side-exit and stock-exit configurations. The Gladiator Bullnose series is engineered to maintain maximum ground clearance.

The company emphasizes its Montana-based production and factory-direct support as differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Exhaust system design and manufacturing", "Patented pulse chamber engineering", "Stainless steel fabrication", "Vehicle-specific fitment development", "Cat-back exhaust configurations", "Side-exit exhaust configurations", "Turndown exhaust configurations", "Exhaust tip production"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Light truck performance parts", "SUV performance parts"], "materials": ["Stainless steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 2018 in Molt, Montana -> db", "Proudly Built in Montana -> /", "40 Years Exhaust Innovation -> /", "Patented pulse chamber eliminates in-cab drone -> description (db) and /", "Limited 3-Year Warranty on all Components -> /", "Stainless Products are Limited lifetime Warranty -> /", "Applications for Ford F-150 2021-2026 and Jeep Gladiator 2020-2026 -> /", "Designed to maintain maximum ground clearance for Gladiator Bullnose -> /", "Factory Support -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Proudly Built in Montana; product listings show manufactured exhaust kits for Ford F-150 and Jeep Gladiator", "founded_year": "2018", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mpi-exhaust-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='MSP Manufacturing operates from Bloomington, Indiana, where it was founded in 1943 by machinists focused on avionics and defense work. The company has remained multi-generational, passing from father to son, and in 2020 Johnny Goode — an Army National Guard veteran with a background in SWAT and law enforcement — became president, steering the shop toward modern automation while retaining its legacy craftsmanship.

The shop provides precision machining, 5-axis milling, 6-axis turning with live tooling, fabrication, welding, mil-spec coating, assembly, and inspection under one roof. Its equipment includes 3- and 5-axis CNC mills with pallet changers, a 6-axis lathe, CMMs, and an AI-assisted CAM system that cuts programming time by up to 80%. Work ranges from single prototypes to production runs in aluminum, steel, brass, titanium, plastics, and Inconel, all tracked through ProShop ERP for full traceability.

MSP serves defense, armory, aviation, medical, and contract-manufacturing customers. Its parts have flown on programs for Boeing, Curtiss-Wright, Bell Helicopter, Gulfstream, and Honeywell, and it supports defense startups and OEMs such as Simtek, Freedom Aero Service, and Ripcord Industries.

The company emphasizes “tight tolerances, zero drama, and people who care,” positioning itself as a partner for high-stakes, high-spec work rather than the largest shop. Veteran-led leadership, in-house finishing and assembly, and a culture of accountability are cited as differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["3-axis CNC milling", "5-axis CNC milling", "6-axis lathe with live tooling", "Prototype and production runs", "Multi-material machining (aluminum, steel, brass, titanium, plastics, Inconel)", "Structural welding (aluminum and steel)", "Fabrication of brackets, enclosures, mounts", "Surface preparation and masking to paint spec", "Mil-spec and industrial-grade coating application", "Mechanical subassembly", "Hardware installation (torque to spec)", "Product labeling and packaging", "Custom kitting and internal part grouping", "Light electromechanical builds", "In-process inspection", "Final inspection with CMM and manual checks", "First Article Inspection Reports (FAIR)", "Serialized part tracking", "ProShop ERP traceability", "Certificate of Conformance (COC)", "CAM Assist AI toolpathing"], "industries": ["Defense", "Armory", "Aviation", "Medical", "Contract manufacturing"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Steel", "Brass", "Titanium", "Plastics", "Inconel"], "equipment": ["3-axis CNC milling machines", "5-axis CNC milling machines with pallet changers", "6-axis lathe with live tooling", "Coordinate measuring machines (CMMs)", "ProShop ERP system", "CAM Assist AI tool", "Inkjet part-marking systems"], "volume": "Prototype to production runs; low-volume high-spec contracts", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Veteran-led, multi-generational ownership", "In-house full process: machining, fabrication, coating, assembly, inspection", "AI-assisted CAM programming reducing programming time by up to 80%", "5-axis machining with pallet changers for complex parts", "Mil-spec and industrial-grade coatings applied in-house",